    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656">

                <pb facs="0781" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg693"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Calderon to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peruvian Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                                C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-05-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 14.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to express to your
                    excellency, in the name of my Government, the gratefulness of the Peruvian
                    people and Government <pb facs="0782" n="694" xml:id="pg694"/> for the message
                    of sympathy delivered by Minister Irving Dudley, in the name of the American
                    people and of His Excellency President Roosevelt, on the occasion of the
                    sorrowful bereavement suffered by Peru.</p>
                <p>Adding my own thanks, it affords me pleasure to renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel Alvarez
                    Calderon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
